{
  "id": "b2-sort-unique",
  "courseId": "cpp-book-02",
  "chapter": 17,
  "title": "Sort before removing duplicate values",
  "level": "Algorithms",
  "prompt": "Return each distinct integer exactly once in increasing order. Do not modify the input. std::unique removes adjacent duplicates only, so put the required operation before it.",
  "signature": "std::vector<int> sortedUnique(std::vector<int> values)",
  "starter": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nstd::vector<int> sortedUnique(std::vector<int> values){auto end=std::unique(values.begin(),values.end());values.erase(end,values.end());return values;}\n",
  "solution": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nstd::vector<int> sortedUnique(std::vector<int> values){std::sort(values.begin(),values.end());auto end=std::unique(values.begin(),values.end());values.erase(end,values.end());return values;}\n",
  "driver": "int main(){std::vector<int> values;for(int v;std::cin>>v;)values.push_back(v);for(int v:sortedUnique(values))std::cout<<v<<\" \";std::cout<<\"\\n\";}\n",
  "sampleInput": "3 1 3 2 1\n",
  "sampleOutput": "1 2 3 \n",
  "tests": [
    {
      "id": "case1",
      "label": "Nonadjacent repeats",
      "expression": "sortedUnique({3,1,3,2,1})==std::vector<int>({1,2,3})",
      "expected": "true",
      "hint": "Sorting makes equal values adjacent."
    },
    {
      "id": "case2",
      "label": "Already sorted",
      "expression": "sortedUnique({-2,-2,0,4})==std::vector<int>({-2,0,4})",
      "expected": "true",
      "hint": "Retain one of each."
    },
    {
      "id": "case3",
      "label": "Empty",
      "expression": "sortedUnique({}).empty()",
      "expected": "true",
      "hint": "Algorithms accept empty ranges."
    },
    {
      "id": "case4",
      "label": "One value",
      "expression": "sortedUnique({7})==std::vector<int>({7})",
      "expected": "true",
      "hint": "Keep the sole value."
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "sort puts equal integers next to one another.",
    "unique returns a new logical end; erase shortens the vector."
  ],
  "explanation": "The precondition for removing all duplicates with unique is that equal values are adjacent. Passing the vector by value copies it, so sorting does not rearrange the caller’s data.",
  "chapterTitle": "Processing Data with Standard Algorithms"
}
